      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High thermal gradients produce coarse, anisotropic microstructures in AlCrFeNiSi builds.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheating the build platform to approximately 350–450°C is an applicable processing window for L-PBF of AlCrFeNiSi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Build-platform preheating reduces the thermal gradient during solidification.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A moderated substrate temperature promotes more uniform nucleation and growth.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10616214::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Build-platform preheating changes the microstructure from columnar grains to a refined, equiaxed grain structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10616214::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The refined, equiaxed microstructure mediates a reduction in residual stress.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A lower solidification thermal gradient reduces residual thermal stresses.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Build-platform preheating slightly slows the cooling rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The slower cooling rate permits enhanced diffusion processes.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced diffusion under the preheated condition produces refined microstructural evolution.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheated AlCrFeNiSi builds will have lower residual stresses than room-temperature-substrate builds.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheated AlCrFeNiSi builds will have a finer and more isotropic grain structure than room-temperature-substrate builds.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10616214::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
